# Derived and personal data — none of it belongs in the repository.
# tools/persoenliche_daten.py holds the personal part of this list as patterns:
# tools/veroeffentlichen.sh, tools/check.sh and the check run on GitHub refuse
# those paths even if someone adds one by force (git add -f). Change both
# together — tests/test_sicherheit_repo.py checks that they agree.

# config.yaml is personal (starting point, weight, gear). Only
# config.example.yaml is versioned; the personal copy is created from it on
# first start and therefore never conflicts when updating. Copies of it
# ("config Kopie.yaml", "config-old.yaml") are just as personal.
config.yaml
/config*.yaml
!/config.example.yaml
cache/
report.html
/report*.html
demo_report.html
ui_defaults.json
/ui_defaults*.json
# The language chosen in the switcher (since 2.1.0) — personal, like ui_defaults.json
sprache.txt
# Memory of the model comparison in the Review — your own checks, personal
modellguete.json
/modellguete*.json
# Session logbook — your sessions, personal like config.yaml (since 1.16.0)
tagebuch.json
/tagebuch*.json
# Your favourite spots — personal like the logbook (since 2.4.0)
favoriten.json
/favoriten*.json
# When saving, the app first writes <name>.neu and then renames it: a
# half-written copy of config.yaml, tagebuch.json, spots.yaml …
*.neu
# Raw exports for importing (Google Takeout, GPX tracks, KML, GeoJSON) are
# personal lists with your own notes — they stay on your computer; the
# repository only holds the import scripts and whatever ended up in the
# catalogue from them
import/*.csv
import/*.json
Takeout/
*.gpx
*.kml
*.kmz
*.geojson
*.zip
live_*.json
live_*.html
# Screenshots and screen recordings show your starting point and your lists
Bildschirmfoto*
Bildschirmaufnahme*
Screenshot*
Screen Recording*
# Backup and swap files of editors
*.bak
*~
.*.sw?
# Local settings and notes for Claude Code
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
# Where the Claude desktop app stores files from the chat — not part of the project
Claude outputs/
.pytest_cache/
tests/_tmp/

# Intermediate files from development runs
*_tmp.html
vorschau.html
